@kyliejenner has had a busy 2026. It's easy, then, to forget that it's only been two years since the launch of the mogul's first fragrance, Cosmic. Now comes an expansion to @kyliecosmetics's scents: the Mood Stones Fragrance Collection.
Featuring three distinct fragrances, this collection was designed to offer a scent for every mood. “I wanted Mood Stones to be an embodiment of my versatility, and for people to be able to honor how they feel in the moment,” Jenner tells ELLE.
To celebrate the launch, we chatted with Jenner about the new Mood Stones collection, astrology, and her favorite scent to wear courtside. Read the full interview at the link in bio.

@emrata is used to shaping fashion trends, but these days, she’s more interested in clothes that simply feel like herself. Take a great pair of jeans, for example, like the ones she wears in @abercrombie & Fitch's fall 2026 denim campaign. Lensed by @cassblackbird and also starring @palomija, the campaign shows Ratajkowski wandering through downtown Manhattan in a rotation of relaxed, low-rise jeans worn in varying combinations that feel quintessentially New York (appropriate, given A&Fs founding on the Lower East Side).
Like many millennials, Ratajkowski came of age during Abercrombie & Fitch’s cultural heyday—but today, she’s embracing its more elevated, modern identity. “I grew up in Southern California, so my style was always really casual,” Ratajkowski tells ELLE, noting her preference for denim and easy basics. “Abercrombie was part of that era for me. I remember having their jeans and loving how effortless they felt, which is still something I’m drawn to today.”
At the link in bio, Ratajkowski reflects on rediscovering the brand, her forever love of denim, and the early-2000s celebrity closet she’d most want to raid.

@wrangler classic workwear jeans are cleaning up nicely. Created exclusively for @wildlifetailor, the relaxed double knees swap standard reinforcement panels for washable cow suede, adding a luxe touch without losing their practicality.⁠
⁠
Available in black and indigo from August 1.

@oakley isn’t simply dropping a new pair of shades. It built them an entire sci-fi origin story.⁠
⁠
The brand’s new Infiniloop model is based on eyewear worn by Jupiter in Book 2 of its post-apocalyptic Future Genesis comic, where the frames help him navigate a storm-ravaged wasteland. In reality, Oakley translates that fictional gear through a futuristic fusion of titanium and O-Matter.

@nike doesn’t want you to choose between comfort and style with its new Studio Fleece and Solo Fleece drop, crowning them as the “ultimate uniform for the everyday athlete.”
Dropping today, the campaign bridges sport and culture with a stacked roster of Nike athletes. Track superstar Sha’Carri Richardson leads the charge, alongside Alysa Liu, Jazzy Davidson, Moses Itauma, and football siblings Lauren and Reece James. Artists Karina and Yeat also step into the mix to showcase the lineup’s versatile, engineered comfort.
Available now via Nike across select regions and globally on September 1.

